Beneficiary Registry

Beneficiaries represent designated recipients of future allocations or distributions.

struct Beneficiary {
    string name;
    uint256 percentage;
    address wallet;
}


Example:

Beneficiary(
    "Katascha White",
    35,
    0x123...
);

Register Beneficiary
function addBeneficiary(
    string calldata name,
    uint256 percentage,
    address wallet
)
    external;


Requirements:

Total allocation cannot exceed 100%.
Wallet must not be zero address.
Beneficiary names should be unique.
Asset Trace System

One of the major distinctions between EONS and ERC-20 is built-in traceability.

Trace Event
event AssetTrace(
    bytes32 traceId,
    string description,
    address indexed actor,
    uint256 timestamp
);

Record Trace
function recordAssetTrace(
    bytes32 traceId,
    string calldata description
)
    external;


Use Cases:

Supply chain records
Financial compliance
Internal audits
Real-world asset tracking
Action Framework

EONS supports custom actions.

Traditional ERC-20 token standards do not provide this capability.

Action Registration
function setAction(
    bytes32 actionId,
    bool enabled
)
    external;

Execute Action
function executeCustomAction(
    bytes32 actionId
)
    external;


Examples:

MintReward
IssueCredential
DistributeDividend
IssueCertificate
ValidateAsset

